##VPC network project

Summary 

This project consists of building a fully custom network from scratch, demonstrating the fundamentals of cloud networking, routing and segmentation.

Steps and cofig details

Step 1:Create the VPC 
Screenshot: 
![Create-my-VPC](https://github.com/Muaz-devops/aws-learning/blob/adf0f1211ad68490ef1ac9f6e5e5fd2f05e0f39e/create-vpc.JPG)

Step 2: Created my Subnets with non overlapping CIDRs and each one in a different AZ
Public subnet screenshot: 
![Subnet-public](https://github.com/Muaz-devops/aws-learning/blob/main/aws-subnet1.JPG?raw=true)
Private subnet screenchot:
![Subnet-private](https://github.com/Muaz-devops/aws-learning/blob/main/aws-subnet2.JPG?raw=true)

Step 3: Created my Route tables (Public/Private) and assigned my Subnets to the corresponding table.
Screenshot:
![public-route-table](https://github.com/Muaz-devops/aws-learning/blob/main/aws-project-igw-route-public-subnet.JPG?raw=true)

Step 4: Created IGW (Internet gateway) and attached to my custom VPC to enable internet access for the assigned resources.

screenshot: 
![attatch-igw](https://github.com/Muaz-devops/aws-learning/blob/main/attatch-igw-to-public-route.JPG?raw=true)

Step 5: Added IGW route to my Public route table
Screenshot:
![Subnet-public](https://github.com/Muaz-devops/aws-learning/blob/main/attatch-igw-to-public-route.JPG?raw=true)
Step 6: Created Security groups (Private/Public) to keep access secure
Screenshot:
![Public-SG](https://github.com/Muaz-devops/aws-learning/blob/main/aws-public-sg.JPG?raw=true)

Step 7: Launch EC2 instances 
Public Subnet Instance: Deployed with a public IP and configured for secure SSH access.
Private Subnet Instance: Deployed without a public IP, acccessible via SSH from Public instance. 

Screenshot:
![SSH-public-to-pirvate](https://github.com/Muaz-devops/aws-learning/blob/main/sshd-into-private-from-public.JPG?raw=true)
